{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The filing entity's membership in the circular's licensed-firm categories requires a separate assessment and is not inferred from platform use.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The specific launch and resumption provisions qualify the general effective-date wording for the post-launch assessment.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected event is an actual STR submission to the JFIU; registration, a technical test, direct contact and automatic record migration are separate event classifications.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Each assessed event has an identifiable submission method. Evidence from separate attempts or resubmissions is not combined to make one event satisfy the selected conditions.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Footnote 3 applies to the XML and prescribed-PDF alternatives carrying its marker. No certificate requirement for the web-based alternative is inferred from this footnote.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a5","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The source establishes a submission-related e-Cert requirement but does not establish that certificate availability alone satisfies it. Signing, authentication, attachment, certificate-holder identity and validity mechanics are not assumed.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a6","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The proposed decision concerns only the selected reporting channel, listed method and footnote 3 condition. It does not establish XML-schema conformity, completion of technical testing, reporting timeliness, substantive STR adequacy or overall legal compliance.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.27994712d6e50c0a1c05dea6.a7","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The blackout urgent-contact instruction and footnote 2 resubmission requirement remain separate. Resubmission does not change the original event's channel or time, and the retained text supplies no resubmission deadline.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.e0c16fb1c5474b508d39720304e54bf8","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The proposed question is whether one in-scope post-launch STR submission satisfies the selected STREAMS 2 channel, listed submission-method and footnote 3 conditions. True would mean that the event used STREAMS 2 and completed one listed method, including the submission-related Hongkong Post e-Cert requirement where XML or PDF was used. False would mean that at least one applicable selected condition failed. Neither an unknown fact nor an unknown or false scope produces a compliance verdict. Formalization is null because the retained source does not specify the certificate relationship needed to interpret the XML and PDF branches without substituting an unsupported operational assumption or an opaque satisfaction fact. No event-level truth value is assigned. This proposed meaning confers no legal approval.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["dependencies"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.338380d99ae44af8af8d286d19cca9ea","issue.d56ed0a6bb434c5785907726a331bab8","issue.0f7fd712e21747029a7d1213ec0e6bea","issue.ac7de1fc1ba6451eb1ab1c3a0e75e3ed","issue.a75154afe2dd4fbba8593c6bc555e953","issue.9f38ea94867045e08de69a1de18caec6","issue.0d85f9f2de564c89a3b61efbc51642c7","issue.41d939d26b944aa3bc0a2e8ce8b4d41c"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The prior models already identify the relevant actors, distinguish channel from method, preserve the launch boundary and separate submission, contact, migration and resubmission events. The consequential remaining defect is the certificate relationship. Model abstraction.c8a341a59885fb7db63017bf makes certificate availability sufficient under an explicit assumption. Model abstraction.ebfcf1c1217258fc2b8613f9 instead requires supply or use 'in the manner required', but the required manner remains unspecified. The retained footnote supports a requirement for the particular submission; it does not resolve availability versus the operational act needed to satisfy that requirement. This proposal therefore withholds a complete compliance formula pending that information. It does not invent a rival signing, attachment or authentication requirement. Splitting the PDF components also prevents the file's format from concealing an incomplete form or a missing upload.","run_id":"run.dcbd61031fd641e78a366a51ca9ca587","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"71c3627a60fbdf7e662cc30b3dae7b8ff95e13a67ad5eade35f0a35874e23663","source_unit_ids":["da12aecad4e68.u0.0","da12aecad4e68.u11.1700","da12aecad4e68.u12.1941","da12aecad4e68.u13.2131","da12aecad4e68.u14.2439","da12aecad4e68.u28.3334","da12aecad4e68.u3.811","da12aecad4e68.u30.3569","da12aecad4e68.u4.1003","da12aecad4e68.u5.1078","da12aecad4e68.u6.1149"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Submission-specific e-Cert requirement without substituting availability or an undefined satisfaction predicate"}